      "alt": "The 1,639 “might have” rows collapse into far fewer engineering concerns:\n\nConcern Historical CVEs\nNative memory-safety boundaries 1,130\nResource exhaustion 148\nPlatform/process isolation 106\nIdentity presentation 97\nInteger boundaries 42\nFilesystem handling 39\nAuthentication 27\nMessage cryptography 23\nMail protocols 18\nMIME/mail parsing 9\n\nThose are not 1,639 separate potential bugs. For example, the 1,130 memory-safety rows mostly repeat native buffer-overflow/use-after-free patterns. Safe Rust eliminates those primitives from our maintained code, but I left them partial because external parsers, codecs, cryptography and small unsafe adapters remain trusted.",
